368 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 210 0 R /Rect [ 56.696999 539.648959 538.585999 745.196963 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure2) /TU (Flowchart illustrating a metadata and ontology management system. The Metadata Parsing Subsystem uses Python to parse metadata from digital assets. It interacts with both the Ontology API and Ontology Manager, both components of the Ontology Subsystem using Python for ontology operations and management. Drupal, using Drupal 10, PHP 8, and JavaScript, receives ontology constraints for form validation and unit conversion. The SPARQL Server, based on Apache Jena Fuseki, stores and queries ontologies, with the Ontology Manager querying it for constraints, data, and unit conversion.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
369 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 210 0 R /Rect [ 56.696999 280.376986 538.585999 477.048007 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure3) /TU (Flowchart depicting a metadata parsing subsystem. Key components include the Metadata Parser Engine, API, Validator, and Registry, all utilizing Python. It interacts with Centralized Asset Storage and the Ontology Subsystem. Drupal is used for uploading and extensions. Arrows indicate processes like parsing, validating, retrieving metadata, and managing ontologies.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
