432 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a six-step process: Initial Information Gathering uses Excel surveys to collect data. Automated Ingestion transforms Excel to CSV and JSON via Python. LLM-Assisted Semantic Mapping aligns domain terms using EMMO and QUDDT, creating enriched CSV. Iterative Expert Validation involves reviewing and revising by experts. Formal Ontology Generation refines CSV and JSON into OWL using a Python script. Publication and Dissemination occur through a persistent URL for distribution.) /K 466 0 R /P 217 0 R /Pg 209 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
433 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a metadata and ontology management system. The Metadata Parsing Subsystem uses Python to parse metadata from digital assets. It interacts with both the Ontology API and Ontology Manager, both components of the Ontology Subsystem using Python for ontology operations and management. Drupal, using Drupal 10, PHP 8, and JavaScript, receives ontology constraints for form validation and unit conversion. The SPARQL Server, based on Apache Jena Fuseki, stores and queries ontologies, with the Ontology Manager querying it for constraints, data, and unit conversion.) /K 467 0 R /P 217 0 R /Pg 210 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
434 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart depicting a metadata parsing subsystem. Key components include the Metadata Parser Engine, API, Validator, and Registry, all utilizing Python. It interacts with Centralized Asset Storage and the Ontology Subsystem. Drupal is used for uploading and extensions. Arrows indicate processes like parsing, validating, retrieving metadata, and managing ontologies.) /K 468 0 R /P 217 0 R /Pg 210 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
435 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart showing the interaction between computational methods: CALPHAD leads to Phase-field, which connects to DFT and interacts with Crystal Plasticity. Crystal Plasticity links to FEM and MD. Arrows indicate the directional interactions between these methods.) /K 469 0 R /P 217 0 R /Pg 211 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
436 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (SPARQL query interface showing a query editor and results table. The editor includes prefixes and a SELECT statement. Results are displayed with columns: class, label, and comment. The query returns 26 results in 0.042 seconds, displaying techniques related to imaging and diffraction.) /K 470 0 R /P 217 0 R /Pg 212 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
437 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Experiment management interface showing a list of four experiments under the 'Experiments' tab. Each experiment, listed under sections 'Name', 'Label', 'Content Type', and 'Actions', includes: 3DEBSD, ACT, APT, and DCT, with corresponding labels and content types. 'View Content Type' buttons are shown next to each experiment.) /K 471 0 R /P 217 0 R /Pg 212 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
438 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (A user interface displaying a field for entering a pulse frequency value of "2" with a dropdown menu for selecting units. The dropdown options include kHz, #/s, failures/s, GHz, and MHz. A software ID field is also shown, allowing the selection or addition of a term.) /K 472 0 R /P 217 0 R /Pg 213 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
